<h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
<p class="page-intro">In short: no cookies, no ads, no tracking across other websites. I count page views anonymously to see which content and tools are used.</p>

<section>
  <h2>Controller</h2>
  <p>Josija Nydegger, Lyss, Switzerland. Contact via <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/josija-nydegger">LinkedIn</a><span class="email-wrap" hidden> or by email at <a class="email"></a></span>.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Visitor statistics with Umami</h2>
  <p>For visitor statistics I use <a href="https://umami.is">Umami Cloud</a> (Umami Software, Inc., USA). The data is stored on servers in the EU. Umami does not set cookies and stores nothing on your device. It records:</p>
  <ul class="bullets">
    <li>the page visited (without the part after <code>?</code> or <code>#</code>, so inputs in the tools are not transmitted),</li>
    <li>the referring website (referrer),</li>
    <li>browser, operating system, device type, screen size and language,</li>
    <li>the country or region, derived from the IP address,</li>
    <li>individual clicks: "URL kopieren" (copy URL) in the tools, passing a load combination to the beam tool, installing the unit converter as an app, downloading PDFs (file name only) and "Save as PDF" on the CV.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The IP address is not stored. To group repeated visits by the same person, Umami creates an anonymous identifier from the IP address, browser details and a regularly changing random value; it cannot be used to identify individuals. If "Do Not Track" is enabled in your browser, nothing is recorded. Ad or content blockers also prevent counting.</p>
  <p>The sole purpose is to improve the website and the tools. The data is not combined with other data and not shared.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>The website is hosted on <a href="https://pages.github.com">GitHub Pages</a> (GitHub, Inc., USA). For every page request, GitHub processes technically necessary data such as IP address, time and requested address, among other things for the security of the service. Details are in <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Tools</h2>
  <p>The tools run entirely in your browser. Inputs are not sent to any server; they are only kept in the address bar (after the <code>#</code>) so that a copied link opens the same values. The pages use your browser's local storage (<code>localStorage</code>) to remember the selected color scheme and some tool settings. This information never leaves your device and can be deleted in your browser settings.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>Links to other websites (e.g. LinkedIn, GitHub) take you to their services, where their privacy policies apply. This website itself does not embed content from other providers, not even fonts.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection (FADP), you can request information about your data as well as its correction or deletion. Since the statistics do not identify individuals, I usually cannot link any data there to you. Feel free to contact me directly with any questions.</p>
</section>

<p class="page-note">Last updated: November 2026</p>
</Base>
